--TEST--
a `name:` call argument is matched against the callee's parameter names, fills exactly one parameter, ends the positional part of the list, and reaches a `Core` member by the spec's own name (`rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2, `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Label {
    public static function render(int $count, string $text): string {
        return $text;
    }
}
// The name has to reach a parameter the callee declares.
echo Label::render(count: 1, caption: "x"), "\n";
// One parameter, one argument: filled positionally and then again by name.
echo Label::render(1, count: 2, text: "x"), "\n";
// Which parameter a positional argument fills is its own place in the list,
// so there is no position left once a `name:` has been written.
echo Label::render(count: 1, "x"), "\n";
// `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2: a `Core` member's parameters are callable by the spec's
// `$name`, so a misspelled one is the same unknown-name refusal as above.
echo Core\Str::repeat(subject: "x", times: 2), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0486]: no parameter of this call can be filled by the name `caption`
  --> case.nvs:8:30
%A
error[E0487]: the parameter `$count` is given an argument twice
   --> case.nvs:10:23
%A
error[E0488]: a positional argument cannot follow a `name:` or `...` argument
   --> case.nvs:13:20
%A
error[E0486]: no parameter of this call can be filled by the name `subject`
   --> case.nvs:16:23
%A
